\end{theorem}

\subsection{A direct connection to structural depth}
\label{sec:fixed-pool-bridge}
The two laws now give a concrete consequence without solving the general
free-correction frontier.  Let $Q_{\rm comp}$ be the common BSC
specialization of \eqref{eq:price-rational-quota}, and let $Q_{\rm pay}$
be \eqref{eq:paid:certificate-numbers}.  A joint sufficient certificate is
\begin{equation}
 Q_{\rm joint}=\max\{Q_{\rm comp},Q_{\rm pay}\},\qquad
 H\ge H_0+NQ_{\rm joint}+K,
 \label{eq:joint-certificate}
\end{equation}
with every original stage admitting $Q_{\rm joint}$ reviews and its
lawful write, report and immediate correction.  Here $H_0$ uses the same
native call accounting in both theorems.  This condition implies both
certificates separately; neither individual certificate is asserted to
imply the other.  It is independent of $f$.

\subsubsection{A rational native-cap bridge at the original risk}
\label{sec:paid:implementation}

\begin{theorem}[Native eight-factor algorithm]
\label{thm:paid:native-eight}
The numbers in \eqref{eq:paid:certificate-numbers} and an explicit rational
algorithm satisfy \eqref{eq:paid:algorithm-sandwich} under
\eqref{eq:paid:cap-certificate}.  The output is an initial mixture of at most
two finite-state policies and bounded calibrated local tests.
\end{theorem}

With probability
\begin{equation}
 \omega_m=\frac{1/2-p_m}{1/2-q_m}
 \label{eq:paid:calibration-weight}
\end{equation}
use that capped test, and otherwise guess blindly.  It has error
exactly $p_m$.  Symmetry gives the same two truth-conditional errors;
all computations use the public channel, not an unknown true bit.

Its mean charge is at most $\mathsf C_{m+1}$, because capping and blind mixing
only reduce that unrestricted mean.  Lemma~\ref{lem:paid:surrogate}'s ratio
calculation gives $\mathsf C_{m+1}\le4\mathsf C_m$ for $m\ge1$.
